# Plan-3 governance artifacts, tracked despite the `docs/` rule above. The territory
# manifest and the four append-only journals are gate inputs: a journal that git silently
# refuses to stage is an unrecorded decision, and append-only enforcement over an
# untracked file enforces nothing. Narrow negations only — the rest of docs/ stays local.
!docs/
docs/*
!docs/plan3/
docs/plan3/*
!docs/plan3/TERRITORY.yml
!docs/plan3/GATE-NAME-RESERVATIONS.md
!docs/plan3/BOARD-VIEW.md
!docs/plan3/PO-QUEUE.md
!docs/plan3/oracles/
!docs/plan3/oracles/**
# A7 fixture modules only — other local evidence under fixtures/ stays ignored.
!docs/plan3/fixtures/
docs/plan3/fixtures/*
!docs/plan3/fixtures/a7-*.mjs
!docs/plan3/fixtures/a16-*.mjs
!docs/plan3/journal/
!docs/plan3/journal/*.md
# BOARD-02: the per-writer board files are the coordination surface between five lanes, and
# an untracked board is a board nobody else can read. Negated explicitly rather than left to
# `git add -f`, because docs/plan3/* silently skips an unnegated path with a hint instead of
# an error — the split's first commit landed the stub while the five files it pointed at were
# quietly dropped, which briefly left the board as a pointer to nothing.
!docs/plan3/board/
!docs/plan3/board/*.md
# Director ruling TB-6: standing policy and PO-sweep findings must carry history,
# diff and attribution. An untracked policy file has no canonical copy — it forked
# across worktrees and a destructive overwrite left no trace.
# Broadened to match the director_paths grant in TERRITORY.yml: governance and
# finding documents are tracked; evidence/, probes/ and worker-reports/ stay local.
!docs/plan3/*.md
# TEST-01 / TEST-02 wire-audit machine artifacts (narrow — not all plan3 JSON).
!docs/plan3/WIRE-AUDIT-FIXED-*.json
!docs/plan3/WIRE-AUDIT-TEST02-*.json
!docs/plan3/WIRE-RUNTIME-PROBES-*.json
!docs/plan3/BACKEND-LIVE-PROBE-*.json
!docs/plan3/TEST01-SKIP-REGISTER-*.json
!docs/plan3/FIXED-WIRE-MARKERS-*.json
!docs/plan3/LEDGER-STATUS-COUNT-*.json
!docs/plan3/TRADE-EVICT-V1-*.json




# PROC-1 (TREE-01), 2026-08-01: these accumulate in the shared main worktree and made it
# impossible to tell a mystery build from a clean one. Checkpoints and evidence are derived or
# archival; scratch probes are throwaway. Ignored so the tree STAYS clean rather than needing
# another sweep.
.ckpt/
_evidence/
# RUN-LOCK-01 holder files: live process state, never content
.locks/
.scratch-*
.scratch-*.tar
.scratch-*.tar.gz

# PASSPORT-3: emitted by bump-chart-engine-build.mjs at image build, carrying the build id and the
# source commit SHA. It is a build output, not source — committing it would let a stale SHA sit in the
# tree and answer for a build that never produced it.
chart v 1.4/chart/build-info.json

# CKPT-01 retained deployable bytes (large JS); manifests/README stay tracked.
artifacts/
!artifacts/ckpt/
artifacts/ckpt/*
!artifacts/ckpt/**/
artifacts/ckpt/**/*
!artifacts/ckpt/**/SHA256SUMS.txt
!artifacts/ckpt/**/README.md
# Wire-audit downloads (multi-MB served modules) — keep local only.
artifacts/wire-*/

# impeccable-ignore-start
# Ephemeral output, runtime state, and per-dev overrides.
# Unanchored: .impeccable may sit at the repo root or under a nested
# workspace (apps/web/.impeccable/...); anchored patterns would miss it.
# Shared artifacts stay tracked: config.json, live/config.json,
# design.json, critique/*.md.
.impeccable/config.local.json
.impeccable/hook.cache.json
.impeccable/hook.pending.json
.impeccable/*.png
.impeccable/live/server.json
.impeccable/live/sessions/
.impeccable/live/previews/
.impeccable/live/annotations/
.impeccable/live/cache/
.impeccable/live/manual-edit-apply-transaction.json
.impeccable/live/manual-edit-events.jsonl
.impeccable/live/manual-edit-evidence/
.impeccable/live/pending-manual-edits.json
.impeccable/live/deferred-svelte-component-accepts.json
.impeccable/live/*.png
# impeccable-ignore-end
